          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>A few years ago, Amazon founder and one of the richest people on earth Jeff Bezos made Dolly Parton the most recent recipient of his Courage and Civility Award. With it came $100 million that Dolly could use in any charitable way she wanted. </p><p><br></p><p>“I try to put my money where my heart is,” she said after receiving the award. “I will do my best to do good things with this money.”&nbsp;</p><p><span style="font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit;"><br></span></p><p>But that was nothing new for the Dolly Llama, whose good deeds were legendary. During her lifetime she gave away countless millions of dollars and proved that she truly was and will forever be the Patron Saint of Appalachia. </p><p><br></p><p>Here are eight times she inspired us with her generosity.</p></div>
